{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., dropping from ~76 to ~68) followed by low-to-moderate sentiment; forecasts consistently overshoot the immediate post-downtrend recovery.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture volatility spikes in the first 5-10 days of the horizon, predicting smooth linear growth while true outcomes show sharp peaks (e.g., +3.5 EUR/day) followed by rapid mean reversion.",
    "Sentiment history is largely ignored; even when sentiment remains near zero or slightly positive during a downtrend, the model assumes continuation of the trend rather than anticipating a reversal spike.",
    "Mean reversion occurs within 10 days of forecast horizon regardless of sentiment direction; models that extrapolate linearly from recent lows significantly overestimate prices before correcting downward.",
    "Horizon-specific error: Models predict a steady climb but true outcomes show a 'spike-and-crash' pattern where the first few days are outliers, followed by a decline below the starting price level."
  ]
}
